{
  "about": "What each parser makes of a pasted link, read by the Go tests (linkshapes_test.go) and the TypeScript ones (client/lib/roomLink or linkKey tests, client/lib/request/requestLink tests). kind share goes to code.ResolveLink and readShareFragment; kind request goes to code.ParseRequestLink and parseRequestLink. A browser parser takes the raw hash, search and pathname of new URL(input). outcome: ok is a whole link (room, and key when the row names one); incomplete is ErrIncompleteLink or a failed parse in Go, and incomplete true or error 'incomplete' in TypeScript; none is a share link that names no room at all, so neither parser joins anything. A row with tsOutcome or tsRoom is a recorded difference between the two parsers, and its finding says why it is harmless. Keyed rows carry no tsOutcome unless a finding says the browser joins nothing. Never a real key or room.",
